From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tile-view <tile-view@localhost>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 06:36:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/23] Mobile: Make the tile notebook filter follow the
 sidebar selection

Previously the notebook filter dialog always offered every notebook,
regardless of what was selected in the sidebar (drawer) -- picking a
tag or a search, or switching notebooks, left the tile view's filter
untouched, so it could easily show notes unrelated to what the
sidebar was pointing at, or stay narrowed to notebooks that no longer
made sense.

The sidebar selection now defines the filter's scope: on a notebook,
the dialog offers only that notebook and its descendants; on "All
notes", every notebook; for a tag, a search, or anything else, the
notebook filter doesn't apply at all -- the filter button is hidden
and the tile list shows state.notes directly, like NoteList does.
Switching the sidebar selection resets the stored filter so the tile
view immediately follows it. Add getScopeFolderIds to compute this
scope, and use it in the toolbar, the dialog and the tile list's
query so a notebook's tiles are always restricted to its own scope,
not just to whatever was left checked in a previous scope. Rename the
dialog's title from "Notebooks" to "Filter".

